    description: "Add a 'hypergumbo install-extras' subcommand that installs every optional dependency the core tool can leverage: gitleaks (existing installer), embeddings (existing installer), rust-analyzer (installer tracked by WI-dotud). --check prints a status table (component / installed / action) analogous to what install-gitleaks --check already does but for the full set.\n\nRationale: the 'happy path' onboarding is currently N separate 'hypergumbo install-X' invocations that nobody runs in order. An install-extras umbrella makes the opt-in story discoverable and lets us mention a single command in the README / CONTRIBUTING docs.\n\nSubcommand behaviour:\n- 'hypergumbo install-extras' → run each installer in sequence, print a summary table at the end (installed / already-present / failed). Non-zero exit if any installer fails; still runs the rest.\n- 'hypergumbo install-extras --check' → status table only, no install. Exit 0 iff all components are present; exit 1 otherwise (so scripts can gate on it).\n- 'hypergumbo install-extras --only gitleaks,rust-analyzer' → subset install (also --skip with the same set for the inverse).\n- Include a matching 'uninstall-extras' that mirrors the existing uninstall-gitleaks / uninstall-embeddings subcommands.\n\nBlocked by WI-dotud (install-rust-analyzer): the umbrella enumerates install-rust-analyzer, so the individual command must exist first. Independent of WI-duzul's analyzer scaffold work — install-extras is pure orchestration over the individual installers."  # 7896
